Falsifies `system_tests::user::unmap_tests::an_unmapped_va_remapped_to_another_frame_survives_the_old_frames_revoke`.

The defect: `AddressSpace::UNMAP` takes the page out of the tables and leaves its record in the
space's mapping log. Every other test of the method stays green, because the tables are right.
The stale record still names `(a, VA)`, so when `VA` is reused for frame `b`, a revoke of `a`
matches the record and unmaps `VA`, which is `b`'s.

Expected to fail: the last assertion, which finds nothing mapped at `VA` where it wants `b`.

diff --git a/kernel/src/syscall.rs b/kernel/src/syscall.rs
index f4089be81..ac322ad9b 100644
--- a/kernel/src/syscall.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/syscall.rs
@@ -1064,7 +1064,8 @@ fn address_space_unmap(name: u64, va: u64) -> Result<i64, Error> {
         // still a window to close, and a record with no page behind it is still a record a later
         // revoke would act on.
         let unmapped = mmu::unmap_user_at(root, va);
-        let forgotten = hold.forget_mapping_at(root, va);
+        let forgotten: Option<u64> = None;
+        let _ = &mut hold;
         if unmapped.is_none() && forgotten.is_none() {
             return Err(Error::BadPointer);
         }
